comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T21:28:31.812Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: all-status searches for init path guard, Windows timeout, and regression lineage reviewed pm-ph3i, pm-wo8, pm-b24b, pm-2kkl, pm-xaib, pm-69nl, and pm-dprb. Each closed item documents shipped historical work; none tracks merged-main run 30220885849's current 44.5-second 15-package init acceptance timeout."
  "2026-07-26T21:28:57.321Z","harness:codex","Root cause evidence: hosted job 89843116382 ran 54 files / 994 tests; 53 files passed, 991 tests passed, two skipped, and this one real multi-process 15-package init acceptance completed in 44.468 seconds after Vitest's 30-second generic limit. No product assertion failed. Canonical pm-ph3i establishes a 60-second explicit budget for genuine install acceptance on hosted Windows."
  "2026-07-26T21:35:33.640Z","harness:codex","Local acceptance evidence: focused real sandbox test passed unchanged in 2.789 seconds; full mandatory lint passed ESLint with zero warnings, jscpd with zero clones, static quality with exact 100 percent docstrings, package boundary, token budgets, SDK surface, import costs, and CLI transport floors. Complete coverage passed 375 files / 6,428 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 (44,306 statements; 31,445 branches; 9,061 functions; 43,045 lines)."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T21:35:34.454Z","harness:codex",Real package-install acceptance combines filesystem work and subprocess startup whose hosted Windows latency can legitimately exceed the generic unit-test ceiling. Preserve semantic assertions and scope an explicit budget to the external-work test only; never raise the suite-wide timeout.
